==================================================================
ROUTE B: universal q<=6 grid window (rigorous, family-indep at rationals)
  maxgap(p/q) >= 1/q > 1/7 for q<=6 for EVERY integer family.
==================================================================
  AP              mu_1/7=0.4425  mass within 1/14 of q<=6 rational=0.4425 (100% of mu)
  GW              mu_1/7=0.5884  mass within 1/14 of q<=6 rational=0.5754 (98% of mu)
  primes          mu_1/7=0.9458  mass within 1/14 of q<=6 rational=0.8982 (95% of mu)
  spreadAP{6+5j}  mu_1/7=0.4427  mass within 1/14 of q<=6 rational=0.4331 (98% of mu)

  => if most mu-mass is near q<=6 rationals for the WORST (near-AP) families,
     the universal grid window is the load-bearing part; saturated/spread
     families get extra mass elsewhere (decorrelation).
